1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,750
A single policy sentence changed.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,700
Which answers are now wrong?

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,818
PolicyDiff Relay traces that change from the source document
to every answer it touched.

4
00:00:07,818 --> 00:00:10,700
The source is a locked Google Doc.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:16,900
When the enrollment age moved from 18 to 21,
a file-scoped Base44 Workflow exported the document.

6
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:21,150
It stored an immutable version, compared it with v4,
and replayed three prior guidance records.

7
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,693
The live control room now shows the completed 3-of-3 incident.

8
00:00:23,693 --> 00:00:28,600
One answer stays valid because it depends on
an unchanged waiting-period clause.

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,550
One is uncertain because the policy never says
whether contractors are applicants.

10
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:36,950
The affected answer cites section 4.2 directly.

11
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:40,382
Reviewers see the old text, new text, model rationale,
and proposed correction together.

12
00:00:40,382 --> 00:00:43,350
The model does not make the decision.

13
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:47,550
Dahunsi approves the correction through
a server-checked reviewer boundary.

14
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:52,400
PolicyDiff locks a new delivery revision,
sends one real Gmail message,

15
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,650
and exposes a single-use acknowledgement link.

16
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:58,571
The recipient confirms it once. Realtime state marks
delivery and acknowledgement complete.

17
00:00:58,571 --> 00:01:02,300
Policy Ops is a restricted Base44 Agent.

18
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,950
It can explain cited evidence and open reviewer work,
but it cannot approve, send, mutate records, or delete.

19
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:12,950
Here it calls the trusted finding tool
and states the contractor gap plainly.

20
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:19,287
The audit export opens a five-minute signed file containing
the version chain, findings, approval, delivery, and receipt.

21
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:24,600
PolicyDiff Relay turns a policy edit
into a traceable correction incident.

22
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:30,046
Seventeen trusted functions. Seven active workflows.
One evidence trail from change to closure.
